split_path(p) is a pure, byte-oriented split of the input string on the single ASCII byte '/' (0x2F), discarding every empty piece. Nothing else: no trimming, no percent-decoding, no normalization, no case folding, no dedup, no dot-segment handling, no other separator.

Exact algorithm (implementable verbatim):

  fn split_path(p: &[u8]) -> Vec<Vec<u8>> {
      let mut out = Vec::new();
      let mut cur: Vec<u8> = Vec::new();
      for &b in p {
          if b == b'/' {                 // 0x2F is the ONLY separator
              if !cur.is_empty() { out.push(std::mem::take(&mut cur)); }
          } else {
              cur.push(b);
          }
      }
      if !cur.is_empty() { out.push(cur); }
      out
